Article 8
(1) Household neglect as referred to in Article 4 letter d constitutes an act of neglecting a person within the scope of one's household;
(2) Neglect as referred to in paragraph (1) also applies to any person who causes economic dependency such that the victim is under the control of that person, by means of:
a. limiting and/or prohibiting decent work inside or outside the home;
b. not providing livelihood; or
c. eliminating access and control as well as participation with regard to economic resources.

