CHAPTER VIII
REHABILITATION AND REINTEGRATION
Article 31
(1) Every woman and child victim of acts of violence has the right to obtain rehabilitation both physical and psychological;
(2) Rehabilitation facilitation services include counseling services, medical psychological, legal assistance and skills training or alternative education;
(3) Every woman and child victim of acts of violence who has recovered both physically and psychologically has the right to be integrated or returned to their family, community and educational institutions for those who are still in school status;
(4) Fulfillment of the integration rights of women and children victims of acts of violence is carried out through cooperation and coordination among all related SKPD, vertical agencies in the region, community organizations, non-governmental organizations and family parties;
(5) Further provisions regarding the implementation of rehabilitation and reintegration are regulated in the Mayor's Regulation.

